# Cline Rules — Deadline Dashboard

## Memory Bank
This project uses the memory bank in `cline_docs/`. Before starting any task, read:
1. `cline_docs/projectbrief.md`
2. `cline_docs/productContext.md`
3. `cline_docs/systemPatterns.md`
4. `cline_docs/techContext.md`
5. `cline_docs/activeContext.md`
6. `cline_docs/progress.md`

Update `activeContext.md` and `progress.md` after completing meaningful work.

## Code Rules
- TypeScript strict; no `any` unless unavoidable.
- All state mutations go through `appReducer` (`src/hooks/reducer.ts`) via typed `AppAction`s — never mutate state in components.
- Pure, testable logic belongs in `src/utils`; side-effectful hooks in `src/hooks`; UI in `src/components`.
- Persist data only via `useAppState` (localStorage key `deadline-dashboard-v2`) or the streak hook.
- Dates are stored as ISO strings.
- Style with Tailwind utilities; include `dark:` variants for light/dark support.
- Run `npm run build` and `npm test` after significant changes to verify.

## No Emojis
- Never use emojis anywhere: UI copy, notifications, toasts, comments, or commit messages.
- Use lucide-react icons, colored dots/badges (e.g. `PaceBadge`), or plain text instead.
